hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2859","Narrated Sa'eed bin Hilal:that Jabir bin 'Abdullah Al-Ansari said: \One day the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out to us and said: \""While I was sleeping I had a vision as if Jibra'il was at my feet. One of them said to his companion: 'Make a parable for him' so he said: 'Listen so that your ears may hear. Hearken so that your heart may understand! The parable of you and your Ummah is but the parable of a king who conquers a land"""""
"2860","Narrated Abu 'Uthman An-Nahdi:from Ibn Mas'ud who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed 'Isha"""""
"2861","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The parable of myself and the Prophets [before myself] is that of a man who constructed a house. He completed it and made it well"""""
"2862","Narrated Al-Harith Al-Ash'ari:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah commanded Yahya bin Zakariyya with five commandments to abide by"""""
"2863","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshār, narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān, from Thābit ibn ʿImāra al-Ḥanafī, from Ghunaym ibn Qays, from Abū Mūsā, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said:\n\n\Every eye is adulterous (zāniyah)"""","""" and when a woman applies perfume and passes by a gathering"""","""" she is such and such\"""""""" — meaning"""","""" an adulteress (zāniyah).\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: There are narrations on this topic from Abū Hurayrah. Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ (good and authentic) hadith.\n\n*Note: This hadith is recorded in Sunan al-Tirmidhī and addresses the broader Islamic principle of modesty and the avoidance of fitnah (temptation)"""","""" emphasizing that the gaze itself is a form of zinā (adultery) of the eyes"""","""" as established in other well-known narrations"""","""" and that a woman going out with conspicuous perfume carries a similar moral weight in terms of the potential for temptation.*"""""""""""
"2864","Narrated Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) narrated: \The parable of the believer who recites the Qur'an is that of a citron"""""
"2865","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The parable of the believer is like the plant; the wind does not stop causing it to sway"""""
"2866","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed there is a tree that does not shed its foilage"""""
"2867","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do you think that if there was a river by the gate of one of you"""""
"2868","Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The parable of my Ummah is that of a rain; it is not known if its beginning is better or its end"""""
"2869","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Buraidah:from his father that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Do you know what the parable of this and this is?\"" - and he tossed two pebbles. They said: \""Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ) know better.\"" He said: \""This (the farther) one is hope"""""
"2870","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Your period in comparison to the periods of the previous nations"""""
"2871","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \People are but like a hundred camels"""""
"2872","Narrated by Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, who said:\n\n\I said"""","""" 'O Prophet of Allah"""","""" what of our private parts should we conceal and what may we expose?' He ﷺ said: 'Guard your private parts"""","""" except from your wife or those whom your right hand possesses (i.e."""","""" female captives/slaves).'\n\nI said"""","""" 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ"""","""" if people are in close proximity to one another?' He ﷺ said: 'If you are able to ensure that no one sees it"""","""" then let no one see it.'\n\nI said"""","""" 'O Prophet of Allah"""","""" if one of us is alone?' He ﷺ said: 'Then Allah is more deserving that one should feel modesty before Him.'\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: *This is a hasan (good) hadith.*\""""""""\n\nSource: Sunan al-Tirmidhi\n\nGrading: Hasan (Good) — as graded by Imam Abu 'Isa al-Tirmidhi"""""""""""
"2873","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The Parable of myself and that of my Ummah is that of a man who kindled a fire"""""
"2874","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out to Ubayy bin Ka'b"
